# HTTPS Configuration for OpenFotoFrame
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Then rebuild: docker compose up -d --build
#
# Display sessions expire after this many seconds (default: 30 days):
# DISPLAY_SESSION_LIFETIME_SECONDS=2592000
#
# Only enable BEHIND_PROXY when the Flask service is reachable exclusively through
# a trusted reverse proxy that overwrites Forwarded/X-Forwarded-* headers. The
# bundled Compose network satisfies this requirement because Flask has no host port.
# BEHIND_PROXY=1
# SECURE_COOKIES=1
# Optional: provide the backend's dedicated CEC machine credential explicitly.
# When omitted, the app generates and persists one in its protected data volume.
# CEC_AGENT_TOKEN=generate-a-long-random-value
# Enable HSTS only for a stable hostname with a publicly trusted certificate.
# Never enable it for self-signed, raw-IP, or localhost access.
# ENABLE_HSTS=1
# TRUSTED_HTTPS_HOSTNAME=photos.example.com
# Decoded-image safety limits (defaults accept normal modern phone photos):
# MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS=80000000
# MAX_IMAGE_DIMENSION=20000
#
# ─── Option 1: Self-signed (default, no .env needed) ───
# Just delete or leave this file empty. Caddy will use self-signed certs.
#
# ─── Option 2: Let's Encrypt via Cloudflare ───
# DOMAIN=photos.example.com
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-cloudflare-api-token
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=your-zone-id          # Enables DDNS (auto-updates A record)
#
# To get a Cloudflare API token:
#   1. Go to https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
#   2. Create Token → Edit zone DNS (template)
#   3. Scope it to your domain's zone
#
# Zone ID is on your domain's Cloudflare overview page (right sidebar, under API).
# If provided, a cron job keeps the A record in sync with your dynamic IP.
#
# ─── Option 3: Let's Encrypt via DuckDNS (free) ───
# DOMAIN=yourname.duckdns.org
# DUCKDNS_TOKEN=your-duckdns-token
#
# To get a DuckDNS token:
#   1. Go to https://www.duckdns.org
#   2. Sign in and create a subdomain
#   3. Copy your token from the top of the page
